From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:11:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 358/358] mfd: macsmc: optionally send the sleep notice from
 the T8132 finisher

Add the bring-up parameter notice_late (default off). With it, the
noirq suspend leaves slpa and the AP idle notice to apple-s2r's T8132
finisher, which calls back right before the commit, and sends nothing
itself; without a T8132 finisher to take it, the notice goes at noirq
as before.

The finisher runs with interrupts off, one CPU and timekeeping
suspended, so the late path takes no lock and uses no clock: one SMC
command at a time, its reply polled for counted 10 us steps (200 ms),
and RTKit's counted AP power notice. It keeps apple_smc_sleep_commit()'s
order and gaps: CLKU for smc-stamp, slpa, 6 ms, the AP idle notice and
30 ms; an idle notice not answered is taken back. The resume reports
whether the notice was sent and how it went; a sleep that stopped before
the finisher's end never sent it, and .complete takes the warning back
as for any refusal.

tools/asahi/smc-notice-late-tests.py checks the parameter, the noirq,
the late path's order and that it is lock- and clock-free, RTKit's
polled notice and the finisher's order from the sources, builds the
counted command against a fake RTKit (reply, timeout after exactly the
counted steps, wrong sequence number, error result), and kills fifteen
mutations.

Assisted-by: LLM
